{# A ribbon of photos that slowly slides to the left, edge to edge (About; Tine, file 63, option A, October 2026).
   It replaced "Then and now" and the photos of "Earlier rounds". Set "ribbonItems" before including this block:
     {% set ribbonItems = friends %}{% include "blocks/photo-ribbon.njk" %}
   Each item: photo (name in src/images/photos, without ending, or its path as the browser editor writes it), year, place, alt. Oldest first.
   Put it in the text column itself (in .prose or straight in a .container), not inside a grid such as .river-pair or
   .card-pair: site.css takes it out of the column to the edges of the screen, measured from the edge of the column.
   Every photo keeps its own shape at one height. The year hangs on it as a sticker, in turn lime, orange, green, blue and
   brown; "Place, year" is written under it and shows again when the photo opens large.
   Without JavaScript, or for people who ask for less motion, it is a strip to swipe, like a gallery on a phone.
   js/ribbon.js makes it slide (and adds the Pause/Play button); the page needs "lightbox: true" for the large photos.
   The dashes inside the tags trim the empty lines around them: on a Markdown page an empty line would end the HTML. #}
{%- set stickerTones = ["sticker-lime", "sticker-orange", "sticker-green", "", "sticker-brown"] -%}
{%- if ribbonItems and ribbonItems.length -%}
<div class="ribbon" data-ribbon>
<div class="ribbon-window">
<div class="ribbon-track">
<ul class="ribbon-list" role="list">
{%- for item in ribbonItems %}
{#- The browser editor writes a path ("/images/photos/name.jpg"); photoSlug makes it the name again #}
{%- set slug = item.photo | photoSlug %}
{%- set meta = photos[slug] %}
{%- set ratio = ((meta.width / meta.height) if meta else 1.5) | round(4) %}
{%- set label = item.place + ", " + item.year %}
{%- set tone = stickerTones[loop.index0 % 5] %}
{#- The photo is 230 px high on a computer and 180 px on a phone (site.css), so the browser picks a file of the right size #}
{%- set sizes = "(min-width: 900px) " + ((230 * ratio) | round) + "px, calc((140px + 10vw) * " + ratio + ")" %}
<li class="ribbon-item" style="--r: {{ ratio }}"><figure class="ribbon-figure has-stickers">
<ul class="stickers" aria-hidden="true"><li class="sticker{% if tone %} {{ tone }}{% endif %}">{{ item.year }}</li></ul>
<a class="lightbox-link ribbon-link" href="/images/photos/{{ slug }}.jpg" data-caption="{{ label }}">{% photo slug, item.alt, { sizes: sizes } %}<span class="visually-hidden">{{ T.openLarger }}</span></a>
<figcaption class="ribbon-caption">{{ label }}</figcaption>
</figure></li>
{%- endfor %}
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ribbon-controls" hidden><button class="ribbon-toggle" type="button" aria-label="{{ T.pauseRibbon }}">{% icon "pause", "ribbon-icon-pause" %}{% icon "play", "ribbon-icon-play" %}</button></div>
</div>
<script src="/js/ribbon.js" defer></script>
{%- endif %}
